06:22:13,080 --> 06:22:16,940
course. Data and metadata should be fair, and knowledge should be machine

4483
06:22:17,040 --> 06:22:17,540
actionable.

4484
06:22:19,040 --> 06:22:22,340
But if we look into that, we all know what fairness means.

4485
06:22:22,400 --> 06:22:24,640
We know how to achieve fairness.

4486
06:22:25,640 --> 06:22:28,740
But we also know that fairness is not a Boolean property.

4487
06:22:28,780 --> 06:22:30,760
It's basically describing a continuum.

4488
06:22:32,040 --> 06:22:35,700
And what you often see is people say, "I made my data

4489
06:22:35,780 --> 06:22:39,420
fair," but what they did is they made the metadata of their

4490
06:22:39,480 --> 06:22:43,260
dataset fair. So they produce fair containers,

4491
06:22:43,800 --> 06:22:46,000
but not necessarily fair content.

4492
06:22:46,700 --> 06:22:49,340
And we believe for many to make

4493
06:22:50,900 --> 06:22:54,320
knowledge actionable, we have to provide fair content.

4494
06:22:54,540 --> 06:22:58,440
So that's the first part. The second, machine

4495
06:22:58,520 --> 06:23:00,820
actionability. Well, if we look at that,

4496
06:23:01,900 --> 06:23:05,620
machine actionability usually means we take information in,

4497
06:23:05,940 --> 06:23:09,780
and a machine transforms it and produces

4498
06:23:09,860 --> 06:23:13,780
some data, information out. That's a data

4499
06:23:13,820 --> 06:23:17,520
transformation process. And often machine actionability

4500
06:23:17,580 --> 06:23:21,400
means allowing data transformation, supporting data

4501
06:23:21,460 --> 06:23:22,760
transformation operations.

4502
06:23:24,340 --> 06:23:26,720
But when we talk about actionable knowledge,

4503
06:23:27,540 --> 06:23:31,380
we also refer to human actionability, and that

4504
06:23:31,440 --> 06:23:35,220
includes different types of processes, operations, not

4505
06:23:35,300 --> 06:23:37,300
only transformation operations.

4506
06:23:38,420 --> 06:23:40,120
So for instance, humans

4507
06:23:40,960 --> 06:23:44,540
have to interact with the world. So they have an

4508
06:23:44,640 --> 06:23:48,440
object given, and they want to designate it to a term.

4509
06:23:48,800 --> 06:23:52,280
Or they have a situation given, and they want to describe it and

4510
06:23:52,340 --> 06:23:53,680
produce language,

4511
06:23:54,900 --> 06:23:58,100
data, representations. That's an epistemic operation.

4512
06:23:58,560 --> 06:24:00,920
And of course, that works the other way around as well.

4513
06:24:01,240 --> 06:24:05,140
We have a term given, and we want to identify, recognize the object.

4514
06:24:05,560 --> 06:24:08,980
And the same with statements. So we have these epistemic

4515
06:24:09,040 --> 06:24:09,760
operations,

4516
06:24:11,160 --> 06:24:14,680
and of course, we have intervention operations, where we have

4517
06:24:15,620 --> 06:24:19,540
material entity going in, and a transformed material entity going

4518
06:24:19,660 --> 06:24:23,020
out. And in between, we have that intervention

4519
06:24:23,080 --> 06:24:23,660
process.

4520
06:24:24,520 --> 06:24:28,320
And I will focus on that type of operation from now on.

4521
06:24:30,040 --> 06:24:33,740
And consequently, neither fairness nor

4522
06:24:33,780 --> 06:24:37,760
machine actionability are sufficient criteria for actionable

4523
06:24:37,820 --> 06:24:40,900
knowledge for such intervention operations.

4524
06:24:42,640 --> 06:24:45,240
So we're dealing with a knowledge action gap,

4525
06:24:46,160 --> 06:24:49,780
and of course, there are many reasons for that, and

4526
06:24:50,280 --> 06:24:54,200
part of that is representational, and that's where I will focus on.

4527
06:24:56,600 --> 06:24:58,000
And there are three challenges.

4528
06:24:58,920 --> 06:25:01,600
The first challenge, it's actionability.

4529
06:25:02,180 --> 06:25:05,680
What practical knowledge is required to achieve a given goal?

4530
06:25:07,440 --> 06:25:11,380
And if we look at our intervention operation-- Oh,

4531
06:25:11,600 --> 06:25:11,900
sorry.

4532
06:25:13,720 --> 06:25:14,760
So we see

4533
06:25:16,880 --> 06:25:18,260
to be successful

4534
06:25:20,528 --> 06:25:24,188
What knowledge do we need? The case of a degraded

4535
06:25:24,248 --> 06:25:26,748
mangrove site turning into an intact one.

4536
06:25:27,548 --> 06:25:31,268
We need procedural knowledge, exactly descriptions,

4537
06:25:31,668 --> 06:25:35,428
directives, what to do step by step towards a

4538
06:25:35,528 --> 06:25:36,688
specific goal.

4539
06:25:39,048 --> 06:25:39,328
That's

4540
06:25:40,188 --> 06:25:43,408
actionability. That's required to be actionable.

4541
06:25:44,908 --> 06:25:47,128
And current FAIR infrastructures typically

4542
06:25:48,228 --> 06:25:51,908
address or represent what is the case, but do not

4543
06:25:51,968 --> 06:25:55,428
provide the procedural knowledge required to intervene

4544
06:25:55,948 --> 06:25:59,708
and transform a given situation into a desired situation.

4545
06:26:01,328 --> 06:26:03,628
The next challenge is applicability.

4546
06:26:04,028 --> 06:26:05,888
Does that knowledge hold here?

4547
06:26:07,328 --> 06:26:10,828
So looking at the same example, we see, well,

4548
06:26:11,768 --> 06:26:13,768
we can plant propagules,

4549
06:26:14,628 --> 06:26:18,608
but we know that this would not always result in an intact

4550
06:26:18,668 --> 06:26:22,288
mangrove site. So we know that actionability

4551
06:26:22,628 --> 06:26:26,588
doesn't equal applicability because of context dependencies.

4552
06:26:28,348 --> 06:26:31,528
So we have to provide applicability conditions.

4553
06:26:32,128 --> 06:26:33,908
So under certain conditions,

4554
06:26:35,428 --> 06:26:38,528
we know this might work, and then you can

4555
06:26:39,848 --> 06:26:40,528
basically

4556
06:26:41,808 --> 06:26:45,288
compare your contextual information with the applicability

4557
06:26:45,348 --> 06:26:47,068
conditions, whether it meets or not.

4558
06:26:47,708 --> 06:26:50,728
This is all just from the representational side.

4559
06:26:52,908 --> 06:26:55,288
The third challenge is auditability.

4560
06:26:55,388 --> 06:26:59,268
So how do we know it works and where has it

4561
06:26:59,348 --> 06:27:00,788
worked and where has it failed?

4562
06:27:02,588 --> 06:27:06,048
So in addition to the applicability conditions, we want to

4563
06:27:06,128 --> 06:27:10,028
have a feedback loop where we get applicability reports

4564
06:27:10,088 --> 06:27:10,328
back

4565
06:27:11,348 --> 06:27:14,968
that can help us to refine these applicability conditions.

4566
06:27:16,568 --> 06:27:17,868
That's auditability.

4567
06:27:19,848 --> 06:27:23,668
So in our example, the mangrove site salinity may

4568
06:27:23,728 --> 06:27:27,108
have fallen outside of the documented success range,

4569
06:27:27,667 --> 06:27:29,628
and if we would have known that before,

4570
06:27:30,508 --> 06:27:33,068
we could have chosen a different

4571
06:27:33,748 --> 06:27:35,728
approach to reach our goal.

4572
06:27:38,448 --> 06:27:40,908
So these three As, they form

4573
06:27:41,868 --> 06:27:43,708
what we call the triple A principle

4574
06:27:45,248 --> 06:27:48,968
of actionability, applicability, and auditability, which are,

4575
06:27:49,808 --> 06:27:50,308
we think--

4576
06:27:52,128 --> 06:27:55,828
first of all, they're nested and there's an order, so applicability

4577
06:27:55,988 --> 06:27:59,108
presupposes actionability, and auditability

4578
06:27:59,268 --> 06:28:01,188
presupposes applicability.

4579
06:28:03,208 --> 06:28:06,788
And we think that these are sufficient and necessary

4580
06:28:07,208 --> 06:28:08,328
criteria for

4581
06:28:09,148 --> 06:28:13,008
the representational side of actionable knowledge, and you can read more

4582
06:28:13,068 --> 06:28:16,848
about that in our paper, which is available on Archive.

4583
06:28:17,288 --> 06:28:17,968
It's a preprint.

4584
06:28:20,348 --> 06:28:22,928
So how can we represent that?

4585
06:28:26,548 --> 06:28:30,468
One possibility to represent that is using what we

